  "limits": [
    "A to B kept the catalog and PhotoExport runtime identical, but its full test executable and ImageEdit runtime changed. The neutral group exercised the existing JPEG route; its timing is a package comparison, not an isolated Swift-only causal effect. B to C held the entire sealed UI bundle constant apart from the catalog runtime.",
    "Two timed samples per arm in each crossover, on one machine; these measurements do not establish population-wide speed or P95. Earlier main 4.795s/0.082s was a separate historical baseline.",
    "The native test removes its temporary catalog at teardown. Native payload and count verification is separate from the per-receipt C ABI replay.",
    "The APFS diagnostic tests close/process interruption, not power removal or a physical external device. Informal clocks that wrote a trace to the same disk were excluded from performance attribution."
  ]
